449\"],\"summary\":\"/proc/<pid>/status shows NoNewPrivs=1 and CapBnd=0000000000000000 (empty capability bounding set), and systemd-analyze security confirms NoNewPrivileges=, CapabilityBoundingSet= and AmbientCapabilities= are all satisfied\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-78fb40e21b1e4266\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 31b01b46-... plus active/enabled service state and current state.json/worker.log data before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-43bfebcca7b544ee\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued via backgrounded nohup; command returned reboot-issued pid before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proves actual restart (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-833ea90dea754a7a\",\"cmd-0846755b51c94831\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out while node was rebooting, then exec succeeded again with boot_id c220ee7e-... (changed from baseline 31b01b46-...) and uptime 0 min\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required service, data, and sandbox constraints (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c02a2cbe10dc4b02\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, inventory-worker.service is active/enabled, worker.log/state.json show fresh ticks resuming from tick=1, and nsenter/proc checks confirm /etc is still read-only and NoNewPrivs=1 persisted\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a systemd-managed, sandboxed background worker named inventory-worker on node1, confirmed it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory and gains no new privileges, then completed the mandatory single-node restart-evidence protocol showing boot identity change and full service/data recovery.","actions_performed":["Created dedicated system user inventory-worker with home /var/lib/inventory (no login shell)","Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh, a POSIX loop that writes state.json/worker.log into /var/lib/inventory every 5s"